DATA NOTICE: diamond

Data files tracked by DVC in this directory (fetch with `dvc pull`):
  data.tar.bz -> ARDB.dmnd, long.fastq.gz, short.fastq.gz
  (ARDB.dmnd and short.fastq.gz are also committed to git here)

What:
  ARDB.dmnd: a DIAMOND-format protein database built from the
  Antibiotic Resistance Genes Database (ARDB). long.fastq.gz (654 MB)
  and short.fastq.gz: Illumina query reads.

Source:
  Benchmark code from https://github.com/bbuchfink/diamond (0.9.10).
  The data are NOT in that repository.

  ARDB.dmnd: built from the protein database of ARDB, the Antibiotic
  Resistance Genes Database (University of Maryland), version 1.1,
  https://ardb.cbcb.umd.edu/ (no longer maintained; its successor is
  CARD). Official download:
    ftp://ftp.cbcb.umd.edu/pub/data/ARDB/ardbAnno1.0.tar.gz
  (ardbAnno1.0/blastdb/resisGenes.pfasta: 7,828 sequences, 3,054,315
  residues). The ARDB.dmnd header records DIAMOND 0.9.10 (build 111),
  7,825 sequences and the same 3,054,315 residues, matching:
    diamond makedb --in resisGenes.pfasta -d ARDB
  run with DIAMOND 0.9.10. A byte-for-byte rebuild has not been
  checked. The DIAMOND port in this directory cannot run makedb.

  Please cite ARDB as: Liu B, Pop M. ARDB - Antibiotic Resistance
  Genes Database. Nucleic Acids Res. 2009;37(Database issue):D443-7.

  Reads: the README here says to contact the HeCBench author for the
  large dataset. short.fastq.gz is the first 500 reads of
  long.fastq.gz. Their origin (Illumina flowcell C9V1HACXX, lane 7,
  barcode ATGTCA) is undocumented.

Copyright:
  DIAMOND: Benjamin Buchfink and contributors. ARDB: created by Bo Liu
  and Mihai Pop, Center for Bioinformatics and Computational Biology,
  University of Maryland (no copyright holder is stated). Reads: unknown.

